From: ghostframe <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:24:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] video_frame: delegate num_planes through PooledVideoFrame

`PooledVideoFrame` forwards every other `VideoFrame` method to its inner
frame -- fourcc, resolution, get_plane_size, get_plane_pitch, map, map_mut,
fill_v4l2_plane, process_dqbuf -- but not `num_planes`, so it silently falls
back to the trait default.

That default derives the count from the fourcc: 2 for NV12. A `VideoFrame`
that overrides it, as any implementation must when the driver reports a
single V4L2 plane for a contiguous format, loses the override as soon as the
frame goes into a pool. `BufferHandles::len()` then disagrees with the queue
and QBUF fails `NumPlanesMismatch(2, 1)`, several layers from the cause.

The same hole opens for any defaulted method added later.
---
 src/video_frame/frame_pool.rs | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_frame/frame_pool.rs b/src/video_frame/frame_pool.rs
index b186b72..7807d59 100644
--- a/src/video_frame/frame_pool.rs
+++ b/src/video_frame/frame_pool.rs
@@ -47,6 +47,10 @@ impl<V: VideoFrame> VideoFrame for PooledVideoFrame<V> {
         self.inner.as_ref().unwrap().resolution()
     }
 
+    fn num_planes(&self) -> usize {
+        self.inner.as_ref().unwrap().num_planes()
+    }
+
     fn get_plane_size(&self) -> Vec<usize> {
         self.inner.as_ref().unwrap().get_plane_size()
     }
